@base = http://localhost:8080

### Real SAP OData metadata
GET {{base}}/odata/$metadata

### Select, filter, stable order, to-one expand and count
GET {{base}}/odata/Movies?$filter=Year ge 2010 and Rating ge 8.5&$orderby=Rating desc&$top=100&$select=Id,Title,Year,Rating,Genre&$expand=Director($select=Name)&$count=true
X-Index-Policy: AUDIT

### Selective indexed filter (ENFORCE should pass after ANALYZE)
GET {{base}}/odata/Movies?$filter=Genre eq 'RareGenre'&$top=10
X-Index-Policy: ENFORCE

### Allowed filter but unindexed column (ENFORCE should reject)
GET {{base}}/odata/Movies?$filter=Title eq 'Inception'
X-Index-Policy: ENFORCE

### Same sequential scan is reported but permitted in AUDIT
GET {{base}}/odata/Movies?$filter=Title eq 'Inception'
X-Index-Policy: AUDIT

### Result budget 75 gives first server page 50, then nextLink gives 25
GET {{base}}/odata/Movies?$top=75&$orderby=Id asc
X-Index-Policy: OFF

### Negative case: top over limit
GET {{base}}/odata/Movies?$top=501

### Negative case: order allow-list
GET {{base}}/odata/Movies?$orderby=Title asc

### Negative case: unbounded recursive expand
GET {{base}}/odata/Movies?$expand=Director($expand=Movies($expand=Director))

### Negative case: aggregation unsupported
GET {{base}}/odata/Movies?$apply=aggregate(Rating with average as AverageRating)

### GraphQL selective filter; variable binding
POST {{base}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json
X-Index-Policy: ENFORCE

{
  "operationName": "Movies",
  "query": "query Movies($genre:String!,$first:Int!){movies(first:$first,filter:{genre:$genre},orderBy:ID){nodes{id title genre director{name}} pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor}}}",
  "variables": {"genre":"RareGenre","first":10}
}

### GraphQL count is inspected too; broad count can be rejected
POST {{base}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json
X-Index-Policy: ENFORCE

{"query":"{movies(first:0){totalCount}}"}

### GraphQL ordering policy rejection
POST {{base}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{"query":"{movies(orderBy:TITLE){nodes{id title}}}"}

### GraphQL explicit budget with server continuation
POST {{base}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{"query":"{movies(first:75){nodes{id title} pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor}}}"}

### GraphQL after: paste the previous endCursor, keep same filter/order
POST {{base}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{"query":"query($cursor:String!){movies(first:75,after:$cursor){nodes{id title} pageInfo{hasNextPage endCursor}}}","variables":{"cursor":"PASTE_CURSOR"}}
